{"format":1,"key":"zone:stonetalon","path":"/lore/zone/stonetalon","name":"Stonetalon Mountains","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"stonetalon","name":"Stonetalon Mountains","path":"/lore/zone/stonetalon"},"levels":"Levels 15-27","description":"The Stonetalon Mountains are a rugged, wind-carved chain of craggy peaks bordering Ashenvale, the Barrens, and Desolace. Revered by both the night elves…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:stonetalon","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["The Stonetalon Mountains are a rugged, wind-carved chain of craggy peaks bordering Ashenvale, the Barrens, and Desolace. Revered by both the night elves and the tauren as a sacred sanctuary, the region's sacred heights stand in sharp contrast to the smoke and machinery choking its lower canyons. Today, the mountains are torn by deforestation, volatile elemental devastation, and simmering border hostilities.","Rising sharply out of central Kalimdor, the Stonetalon range catches the moisture drifting from the western seas, giving birth to sudden downpours and treacherous, rain-slick sandstone trails. The dominant feature of the lower valleys is the incessant scouring gale known as the Ill Winds, capable of blinding travelers with grit or throwing the careless straight off sheer cliffsides. Higher up, evergreen forests mantle the ridges surrounding Stonetalon Peak, where the night elves tend ancestral barrows and glades, watching over the sacred roosts of wyverns and hippogryphs that nest along Mirkfallon Lake.","The peaceful solitude of the range has been violently disrupted by the arrival of the Venture Company. Setting up sprawling logging camps and digging deep strip mines in Windshear Crag, the goblins—aided by the deranged leper gnome Gerenzo Wrenchwhistle—have clear-cut old-growth timber, blackened the skies with furnace smoke, and poured industrial sludge into the mountain runoff. Their greed has provoked swift retaliation: local shamans from Orgrimmar answered the agonized cries of the mountain spirits, while small Alliance camps stationed nearby fight back against the defilers to protect what remains of the highlands.","To the south lies the Charred Vale, once a blossoming wilderness, now reduced to an ash-covered wasteland churning with rogue fire elementals, black dragonspawn, and harpies. While the peaks were the historic site where the Horde and Alliance forged an uneasy truce during the Third War under the guidance of the mysterious Oracle, current relations are fraying. Renegade Grimtotem tauren operate out of seized encampments, and Darkspear trolls in Malaka'jin clash with Alliance incursions pushing outward from the Barrens and Ashenvale."],"hash":"71506c","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"3eb9217524","sec":126},"female-narrator":{"sha":"2dbcee4a26","sec":133}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Stonetalon Mountains (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stonetalon_Mountains_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Stonetalon Mountains","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stonetalon_Mountains"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/stonetalon-peak","n":"Stonetalon Peak","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/sun-rock-retreat","n":"Sun Rock Retreat","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/windshear-crag","n":"Windshear Crag","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/charred-vale","n":"Charred Vale","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/malaka-jin","n":"Malaka'jin","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/ashenvale","n":"Ashenvale","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/barrens","n":"The Barrens","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/desolace","n":"Desolace","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1701-fire-hardened-mail","n":"Fire Hardened Mail","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/charred-horn","n":"Charred Horn","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/item/furen-s-instructions","n":"Furen's Instructions","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/item/galvanized-horn","n":"Galvanized Horn","k":"item"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/blackwolf-river","n":"Blackwolf River","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lor